{"kind":"propose","text":"E3 row typing adds a second compatibility finding. A declared pending open can write a self-reference. The speculative projection represents that item value as an exact symbolic source, while the existing C4 Row type represents item values as numbers. Adding symbolic values under the approved Row intersection would expose the wrong public type. No current production adopter was found, but a typed SDK consumer can rely on the numeric value. I propose retaining the existing C4 row and rows unchanged and exposing the E3 projection in a distinct synchronous projected row and rows surface on ClientView. Its verified rows carry refs and truthful ActRow item values, including symbols. It carries the previously proposed modern unavailable arm and the approved legacy custody arm. ClientView explore and offers stay synchronous at the same cut. Please decide whether to use the separate projection before changing the public type."}